-- חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ג/10 (8.8.2023): עדכון סמלי שאלונים בבחינת הבגרות במתמטיקה.
-- The matriculation-preparation bonus (גמול הכנה לבגרות) in mathematics for
-- the questionnaire codes added in תשפ"ג: a table, by questionnaire, of the
-- bonus before the reform and under it (external and school-based parts).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

-- not weighed against `the Equal Pay Law`: the words the search found are
-- not on its subject: ‘אב’ is the month of Av in a date; none gives pay or
-- other remuneration by sex.

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשפ"ג/10`

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 akn:preamble/p10 akn:preamble/p11 The letterhead, date, reference number, circular number, addressee (the owners of upper-division institutions), greeting and subject line; no rule.

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 A pointer: the circular follows circular תש"פ/10 (linked), on the new matriculation examination plan in the upper divisions, which sets who is paid the bonus and on what; its rules are not restated here, and this circular only adds rows to its table (¶15).

-- ¶14: in תשפ"ג questionnaire codes were added to the mathematics
-- matriculation examination in the upper divisions.
@ref akn:hc_1/p3
`the school year the codes were added in` MEANS "תשפ\"ג"

-- akn:conclusions/p1 akn:conclusions/p2 akn:conclusions/p3 akn:conclusions/p4 akn:conclusions/p5 akn:conclusions/p6 akn:conclusions/p7 akn:conclusions/p8 akn:conclusions/p9 akn:conclusions/p10 akn:conclusions/p11 akn:conclusions/p12 akn:conclusions/p13 akn:conclusions/p14 akn:conclusions/p15 akn:conclusions/p16 akn:conclusions/p17 akn:conclusions/p18 akn:conclusions/p19 akn:conclusions/p20 akn:conclusions/p21 akn:conclusions/p22 akn:conclusions/p23 akn:conclusions/p24 akn:conclusions/p25 akn:conclusions/p26 akn:conclusions/p27 akn:conclusions/p28 akn:conclusions/p29 akn:conclusions/p30 akn:conclusions/p31 akn:conclusions/p32 akn:conclusions/p33 The sign-off, the signatory and the list of copies, which the page prints between the letter and its table; no rule.

§§ `שאלוני בחינת הבגרות במתמטיקה`

@desc The two bonus columns of the table: the bonus before the reform, and under it.
DECLARE `bonus regime` IS ONE OF
    `before the reform`
    `under the reform` @desc the matriculation bonus as circular תש"פ/10 sets it under the reform, split into an external part (70%) and a school-based part (30%)

@desc One cell of the table's bonus columns: blank, or a bonus in weekly hours (ש"ש) and in percent.
DECLARE `bonus cell` IS ONE OF
    `blank cell`
    `bonus of` HAS
        `bonus weekly hours` IS A NUMBER
        `bonus percent`      IS A NUMBER @desc as a fraction: 0.02 is 2%

@desc One printed row of the table: the questionnaire, its codes, the units, the bonus before the reform and under it, and the remark.
DECLARE `questionnaire row of circular תשפ"ג/10` HAS
    `questionnaire`            IS A STRING
    `codes`                    IS A LIST OF STRING
    `units`                    IS A NUMBER  @desc study units (יח"ל); the page prints it once for the rows of its group
    `bonus before the reform`  IS A `bonus cell`
    `reform external bonus`    IS A `bonus cell` @desc the external matriculation part (70%)
    `reform school-based bonus` IS A `bonus cell` @desc the school-based matriculation part (30%)
    `remark`                   IS A STRING

-- ¶15: for the avoidance of doubt, the matriculation-preparation bonus in
-- mathematics for these questionnaires too, as tabulated. The table as
-- printed (¶48-¶76): the corpus carries it as lines of prose, not as a
-- table (a corpus defect); the cells below are read in the order the corpus
-- prints them. For questionnaire 801 the reform bonus sits in the
-- school-based column, which the remark beside it confirms ("the
-- school-based matriculation is questionnaire 35183"); for every other row
-- the reform bonus is in the external column. "מתמטיקה" carries an
-- asterisk that no note on the page answers.
@ref akn:hc_1/p4 akn:unheaded_1__hc_1/p1 akn:unheaded_1__hc_1/t1
`the mathematics questionnaires table` MEANS
    LIST `questionnaire row of circular תשפ"ג/10` "801"     (LIST "035183", "035173") 3 (`bonus of` 0.5 0.02)  `blank cell`         (`bonus of` 0.5 0.02) "הבגרות הבית ספרית הינה שאלון 35183",
         `questionnaire row of circular תשפ"ג/10` "802"     (LIST "035381", "035371") 3 (`bonus of` 0.5 0.02)  (`bonus of` 0.5 0.02)  `blank cell`         "",
         `questionnaire row of circular תשפ"ג/10` "803"     (LIST "035382", "035372") 3 (`bonus of` 1 0.02)    (`bonus of` 1 0.02)    `blank cell`         "",
         `questionnaire row of circular תשפ"ג/10` "804+803" (LIST "035481", "035471") 4 (`bonus of` 2 0.04)    (`bonus of` 2 0.04)    `blank cell`         "",
         `questionnaire row of circular תשפ"ג/10` "805"     (LIST "035482", "035472") 4 (`bonus of` 1 0.02)    (`bonus of` 1 0.02)    `blank cell`         "",
         `questionnaire row of circular תשפ"ג/10` "806+805" (LIST "035581", "035571") 5 (`bonus of` 2.25 0.04) (`bonus of` 2.25 0.04) `blank cell`         "",
         `questionnaire row of circular תשפ"ג/10` "807"     (LIST "035582", "035572") 5 (`bonus of` 1.25 0.02) (`bonus of` 1.25 0.02) `blank cell`         ""

GIVEN `code` IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF `questionnaire row of circular תשפ"ג/10`
DECIDE `the rows for code` `code` IS
    filter (GIVEN r YIELD elem `code` (r's `codes`)) `the mathematics questionnaires table`

-- The bonus the table gives a questionnaire code, by regime. Under the
-- reform the external and school-based parts are both listed; which part a
-- teacher is paid on is circular תש"פ/10's rule, not this one's.
GIVEN `code` IS A STRING, `regime` IS A `bonus regime`
GIVETH A LIST OF `bonus cell`
DECIDE `the bonus cells for` `code` `regime` IS
    CONSIDER `regime`
    WHEN `before the reform` THEN map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `bonus before the reform`) (`the rows for code` `code`)
    WHEN `under the reform` THEN concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD LIST r's `reform external bonus`, r's `reform school-based bonus`)
                                              (`the rows for code` `code`))

GIVEN c IS A `bonus cell`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weekly hours of circular תשפ"ג/10 of` c IS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `bonus of` h p THEN h
    WHEN `blank cell` THEN 0

GIVEN c IS A `bonus cell`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `percent of` c IS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `bonus of` h p THEN p
    WHEN `blank cell` THEN 0

@export The mathematics matriculation-preparation bonus that circular תשפ"ג/10 lists for a questionnaire code, in weekly hours (ש"ש), before the reform or under it (the external and school-based parts added)
GIVEN `code` IS A STRING @desc the questionnaire code as printed, e.g. "035381"
      `regime` IS A `bonus regime` @desc before the reform, or under it
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `bonus weekly hours for code` `code` `regime` IS
    sum (map `weekly hours of circular תשפ"ג/10 of` (`the bonus cells for` `code` `regime`))

GIVEN `code` IS A STRING, `regime` IS A `bonus regime`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `bonus percent for code` `code` `regime` IS
    sum (map `percent of` (`the bonus cells for` `code` `regime`))

-- Every printed code is in exactly one row.
`every printed code` MEANS concat (map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `codes`) `the mathematics questionnaires table`)
#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD count (`the rows for code` c) EQUALS 1) `every printed code`
#ASSERT count `every printed code` EQUALS 14

-- In every row the bonus under the reform equals the bonus before it — the
-- table changes the questionnaires, not the bonus.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD `bonus weekly hours for code` c `before the reform` EQUALS `bonus weekly hours for code` c `under the reform`
                       AND `bonus percent for code` c `before the reform` EQUALS `bonus percent for code` c `under the reform`)
            `every printed code`

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples, from the table.
#ASSERT `bonus weekly hours for code` "035183" `under the reform` EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `bonus percent for code` "035481" `before the reform` EQUALS 0.04
#ASSERT `bonus weekly hours for code` "035571" `before the reform` EQUALS 2.25
#ASSERT `bonus weekly hours for code` "035999" `before the reform` EQUALS 0

§§ `Property checks`

-- The table over every printed row and code, and over codes the table
-- does not print.

`every regime of circular תשפ"ג/10` MEANS LIST `before the reform`, `under the reform`

GIVEN c IS A `bonus cell`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is blank` c IF
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `blank cell` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Every row: a bonus before the reform, and under it exactly one of the two
-- parts (the school-based one only for 801, as its remark says); 3 to 5
-- units; two codes; a bonus of ½ to 2¼ weekly hours at 2% or 4%.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN r YIELD
                    NOT `is blank` (r's `bonus before the reform`)
                AND (`is blank` (r's `reform external bonus`)) EQUALS NOT `is blank` (r's `reform school-based bonus`)
                AND (NOT `is blank` (r's `reform school-based bonus`)) EQUALS (r's `questionnaire` EQUALS "801")
                AND r's `units` AT LEAST 3 AND r's `units` AT MOST 5
                AND count (r's `codes`) EQUALS 2
                AND `weekly hours of circular תשפ"ג/10 of` (r's `bonus before the reform`) AT LEAST 0.5
                AND `weekly hours of circular תשפ"ג/10 of` (r's `bonus before the reform`) AT MOST 2.25
                AND elem (`percent of` (r's `bonus before the reform`)) (LIST 0.02, 0.04))
            `the mathematics questionnaires table`

-- Every printed code, in each regime: a bonus that is positive and is its
-- one row's; a code the table does not print gets nothing in either.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD
                all (GIVEN g YIELD
                            `bonus weekly hours for code` c g GREATER THAN 0
                        AND count (`the bonus cells for` c g) EQUALS (IF g EQUALS `before the reform` THEN 1 ELSE 2))
                    `every regime of circular תשפ"ג/10`)
            `every printed code`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN c YIELD
                all (GIVEN g YIELD
                            `bonus weekly hours for code` c g EQUALS 0
                        AND `bonus percent for code` c g EQUALS 0)
                    `every regime of circular תשפ"ג/10`)
            (LIST "035183 ", "35183", "035999", "035171", "")
